# secrets
.env

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# output
out/
proj_*/
*.egg-info/

# big things that do not belong in history
node_modules/
_to_delete/
.firebase/
*.tgz
*.zip
*.pt
*.onnx
# ...and the other two shapes a checkpoint arrives in. `dbpp_coo.dat` is 116MB
# and `detect-20241225.ckpt` is 308MB, and GitHub REFUSES a file over 100MB -
# so without these two lines the first push of the week fails on the upload
# rather than on anything you could fix in a commit. Weights are downloaded by
# `get_models.py`; they are not source.
*.dat
*.ckpt
models/
firestore-debug.log

# Generated, and large. `site/index.html` IS tracked — it is what Firebase
# serves and it is 46KB — but the standalone copy is that same page with three
# megabytes of pictures inlined, so committing it makes every rebuild a
# three-megabyte diff of base64. `python site/build.py` writes one whenever you
# want one.
site/mangatct-site-standalone.html

# scratch
diag_*.png
*.log

# Top-level scratch. Everything in this project that starts with ONE
# underscore at the root is a working copy or a tarball -- `_pj.py` and
# `_ct.py` are stale duplicates of project.py and detect/comictext.py,
# `_editor.html` and `_sheet.png` are leftovers, `_to_delete/` is where
# files go because the device bridge cannot delete them.
#
# `[!_]` is what keeps `__init__.py` and `__main__.py`: they start with
# TWO, and they are real source.
/_[!_]*

# The push script's own noise, if it ever writes any.
push.log
